# Beam along its span

Bending moment and deflection of a simply supported beam at tenths of the span,
and the governing section found by a small program.

```calc
L := 6 m
q := 12 kN/m
EI := 210 GPa*8360 cm^4
```

## Along the span

```calc
i := 0..10
x[i] := i*L/10
M[i] := q*x[i]*(L - x[i])/2
δ[i] := q*x[i]*(L^3 - 2*L*x[i]^2 + x[i]^3)/(24*EI)
M = ? kN*m   #= [0; 19.4; 34.6; 45.4; 51.8; 54.0; 51.8; 45.4; 34.6; 19.4; 0]*kN*m
δ = ? mm     #= [0; 3.62; 6.85; 9.38; 11.0; 11.5; 11.0; 9.38; 6.85; 3.62; 0]*mm
```

## Governing section

```calc
peak(v) :=
  k <- 0
  for j in 0..last(v)
    k <- j if v[j] > v[k]
  k
k_max := peak(M) = ?   #= 5.00
x[k_max] = ? m         #= 3.00 m
max(M) = ? kN*m        #= 54.0 kN*m
```

## Diagrams

```plot {#p1 w=480 h=260}
x: 0 m .. L
traces:
  - y: q*x*(L - x)/2
    unit: kN*m
    label: Bending moment
  - y: q*(L/2 - x)
    unit: kN
    label: Shear
    axis: right
    style: { line: dash }
```
